# Security for OCT extensions

OCT installs extensions with a cluster admin's credentials, so every extension is
trusted code. Keep what it can do small and say why it needs it. Reference:
`oct-storefront/docs/security-model.md`.

## Declare

- Add `spec.security` to the catalog entry: `level`, `summary`, and a `why` for each
  RBAC rule, Route, egress host and runtime-created object. The install review shows
  these reasons; CI warns when the manifests do more than the declaration says.

## Permissions

- Ask for the least RBAC that works. Prefer a Role in the tool's namespace over a
  ClusterRole. No `*` verbs, resources or API groups. No `escalate`, `bind`,
  `impersonate`, cluster-wide Secret reads, or bindings to cluster-admin/admin/edit.
- Creating an SCC or other cluster-scoped security object at runtime must be declared
  in `spec.security.privileged.runtimeCreates` with how it is cleaned up.

## Backends

- Use `backend-security-kit`: one `auth.Route` per handler, each with the permission
  the caller needs. Never expose a route that acts with the ServiceAccount on behalf of
  an unchecked caller. Public routes only for things that must work without a user.
- The ConsolePlugin proxy sets `authorization: UserToken`.
- New backends ship `AUTH_MODE=enforce`. Migrated backends ship one release in audit.
- Validate every caller-supplied name, namespace, path and argument (`validate`).
  Never run `sh -c` with caller input; pass the program and arguments directly.
- Verify TLS (no `InsecureSkipVerify`), no CORS headers, HTTPS with the service-ca cert.

## Network

- Default to console-only. A Route publishes a service outside the cluster: expose
  only the path that needs it, on its own listener, and declare why.
- Ship a NetworkPolicy that admits only the console (and probes) to the backend;
  catalog rows with one set `versions[].minStorefront: "1.6.0"`.

## Secrets and images

- Never put credentials in a manifest, image, ConfigMap, log or catalog entry.
  Reference a Secret the admin creates, or create it at runtime from user input.
- Public images with version tags (never `:latest`); pin by digest for releases.
- Containers: non-root, `allowPrivilegeEscalation: false`, drop ALL capabilities,
  `readOnlyRootFilesystem: true` with emptyDir scratch space, and
  `automountServiceAccountToken: false` when the pod doesn't call the API. No `chmod 777`.

## Check

- `yarn check-repo` (security patterns; `CHECK_REPO_SECURITY=error` to fail on them)
  and, in oct-storefront, `yarn security-check`.
